  "steps": [
    "Potatoes. Preheat the grill to 400–425 °F for indirect cooking. Scrub, pierce, rub with oil and salt, wrap in foil and grill 45–60 minutes until tender.",
    "Herb butter. Melt the butter, add garlic for 30 seconds, then stir in the herbs and salt. Set aside.",
    "Steak bites. Toss the steak with oil, salt, pepper and seasoning. Sear in a very hot cast iron skillet on the grill 2–3 minutes per side for medium-rare. Drizzle with 1 tbsp herb butter.",
    "Filling. Cut the potatoes lengthwise ¾ of the way through and squeeze the ends to open. Mix sour cream, cheese, chives, salt and pepper.",
    "Load. Fill the potatoes, top with steak bites and drizzle with the remaining herb butter. Garnish with chives and serve hot."
  ],
